  "recipeDetail": "Comments from the Creator\nThis recipe was inspired by the atmosphere of rural Japan. It brings out the simple warmth of wooden tableware, earth, and greenery, while keeping highlights from becoming too bright and preserving elements such as the natural tones of skin and the texture of white rice. It’s ideal for gently capturing simple scenes from everyday life, much like life with a wood-fired oven. It works beautifully on sunny days, as well as in dappled sunlight and on overcast days. Try adjusting the exposure and white balance to suit the scene and your preferred look.",
